Data analytics can be used to prevent fraud and security breaches by detecting potential vulnerabilities and suspicious activities in real-time. By monitoring data continuously, analytics tools can identify potential issues before they turn into a full-blown problem, allowing organizations to take proactive steps towards prevention. For example, data analytics can be used to detect anomalous login patterns or unusual movement of large amounts of data, indicating a potential insider threat or cyber attack. Similarly, analytics can be used to monitor financial transactions for potential fraud, such as detecting an unusually high number of refund requests or a sudden increase in the number of new accounts.

